WEBVTT

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:28.470
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:28.470
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:28.470
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.030 --> 00:02:02.460
Chapter XIV

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:14.050
The distant beginning of all this may lie in the fact that a man named Martin Otto von Siegmeister...

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:19.060
...was born the son of a Department of Public Order Maintenance bureaucrat, in the Ministry of the Interior.

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:26.960
His father inherited a barony
and held the title of <i>Reichsritter...</i>

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:30.760
...but as someone from the
bottom of aristocratic society...

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:34.630
...he must've put a lot of effort into maintaining his pride as an aristocrat, unlike those highly ranked in society.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:39.940
Siegmeister's father must have found his raison d'etre as an Imperial aristocrat...

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:44.430
...after being placed in the Ministry of the Interior's Department of Public Order Maintenance...

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:49.500
...by persecuting commoners who sympathized with such "unacceptable" philosophies like republican democracy.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.310
He was a diligent worker...

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:55.400
...and always eclipsed his colleagues in the number of thought offender arrests...

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:58.000
...confessions obtained by torture, and other such categories.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:03.370
Even his colleagues were said to be
disconcerted by his tenacity and relentlessness.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:06.760
He apparently brought home
literature on republican democracy...

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:12.400
...which he had confiscated from thought offenders and studied them to "know the enemy."

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.870
As a result, his home 
housed many "forbidden books."

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:19.560
And ironically, but quite naturally...

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.660
...Siegmeister's son came in contact
with those "forbidden books."

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:27.310
Perhaps he{i.e. Siegmeister} began to lean toward republican democracy...

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.770
...partially because he was
repelled by his father...

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:33.160
...who was a gloomy degenerate at home,
with a tendency for domestic abuse.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.960
Though it also goes without saying, those "forbidden books" opened his eyes to see social injustice.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.060
Thus, young Siegmeister apparently
decided to devote himself...

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:47.800
...to the cause of changing the unjust society of the Galactic Empire.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.010
But in the Galactic Empire...

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:55.500
...it could endanger his life to publicly
disagree with present political philosophy.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:59.830
Being cautious, Siegmeister kept his republican democracy philosophy inside his head...

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:02.610
...and outwardly graduated
from military school...

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:05.220
...later earning numerous promotions in the military organization.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.610
Siegmeister, instead of being
a combat commander...

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:11.100
...seemingly possessed
an unrivaled talent as an organizer.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.610
Shrewdly and deliberately...

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:17.570
...he began to create his own organizational
network within the Galactic Empire's military.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:22.610
While the father grew older,
and more and more degenerate...

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:26.320
...intensifying his persecution
of thought offenders...

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:31.710
...the son was silently plugging the holes that the father dug.{made.}

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:40.690
That's a chilling father-and-son relationship.

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:41.810
Yeah.

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:48.460
In Imperial Year 408, somewhat
symbolically the year his father died...

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:51.590
...Siegmeister gained a
cohort named Michaelsen.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:55.210
Michaelsen was a successor
to a baronial family...

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.690
...but as a result of conflict with
relatives over the inheritance...

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:01.410
...he seemed to have become wary of aristocratic society.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:09.160
But Michaelsen apparently wasn't as firm in his convictions and beliefs as Siegmeister...

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:12.460
...but seemed to find his reward
by securing a position of power...

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:16.460
...and wielding authority
within the secret organization.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:23.710
In other words, a reward as an artist{or creator} - that may have been the source of his passion.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:28.780
The thing that Siegmeister started was completed by Michaelsen.

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:32.610
In the history of the Galactic Empire...

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:35.880
...it must have been the most competent and dangerous unpatriotic espionage network ever created.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:39.910
Since the military police
and Public Order Maintenance...

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:42.550
...were as active during this
period, just as they are today...

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:46.640
...you can guess how effective their{i.e. Siegmeister's organization} underground movement was.

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:53.660
Eventually, Siegmeister began thinking 
about defecting to the Free Planets Alliance.

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:56.160
He had always been attracted
to the nation of freedom...

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:00.300
...and the organization he built
was in good hands with Michaelsen.

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:04.460
More than anything else, the loss of his wife and daughter in a fire at a resort hotel...

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:07.260
...apparently severed his last
attachment to his native country.

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:16.410
In Imperial Year 419, Space Year 727, 
Admiral Siegmeister, 46 years old at the time...

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:20.310
...asked to be assigned to the front lines and returned to the battlefield for the first time in 5 years.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:24.540
And from the front lines, he himself piloted a shuttle and escaped.

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:26.910
Evading the pursuit of the Imperial Force, which had realized his intentions...

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:31.740
...he finally arrived at the Alliance's patrol lines after 8 days of solitary flight.

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:34.910
After defecting, Admiral Siegmeister...

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:40.520
...willingly cooperated with the Alliance government in order to realize his own convictions.

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:45.650
He believed that the Alliance government was the ideal political embodiment of freedom and equality.

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:51.670
That sincerity and integrity of his was something the Alliance government easily took advantage of.

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:57.510
Between Space Year 728 and 738...

00:06:57.510 --> 00:07:01.910
...Siegmeister was given a branch room within the Joint Chief of Staff Headquarters...

00:07:01.910 --> 00:07:03.810
...and from there,
across 10,000 light years...

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:07.260
...directed the espionage network
within the Empire by long distance.

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:12.460
His contributions couldn't
be recognized openly...

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:15.060
...so even the existence of this
branch room was not made public.

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:18.410
Even then, the Alliance government...

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:21.690
...treated Siegmeister as favorably as
it could under the circumstances.

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:27.920
They treated him as a Vice Admiral with a high salary, a grand official residence, along with a lordly title.

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:32.430
But time gave him
knowledge and disappointment.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:36.860
He was able to see the blemishes 
of the Alliance underneath the make-up.

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:41.510
Needless to say, the Alliance was not an ideal government, but rather a realistic existence...

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:45.260
...holding corruption and contradictions within itself - a fact which he was forced to realize.

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:52.020
Siegmeister was disappointed in the Alliance, but couldn't simply re-defect for that reason...

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:58.910
...and, with the heartbreak of an idealist who was betrayed by reality, he spent his days in discontent.

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:04.650
But in 738, a new star of
hope appeared before him.

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:09.960
That was the 730 Mafia.

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:17.510
Having led the Alliance to complete victory in the battle in Phiazard Starzone...

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:20.600
...the 730 Mafia
came to his attention.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:27.910
Bruce Ashbey, Alfred Rosas,
Frederick Jasper, Wallice Warwick...

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:33.360
...Fang Tchewling,
John Drinker Cope, Vittorio di Bertini...

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:37.800
...each of them still younger than 30, they were a glittering group of talented men.

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:44.160
Just as the people of the Free Planets Alliance became their fans, Siegmeister, at the age of 56...

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:45.500
...must have also been attracted to them.

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:50.510
He determined to gamble his dream on these young brilliant talents of the Alliance Force.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:54.610
Since he was former military...

00:08:54.610 --> 00:09:00.300
...it was only natural that he looked to the military as a force to change the present predicament.

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:05.150
His belief in the re-governance of the
universe under a republican democracy...

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:09.160
...and that this group of young, dignified knights
would be the ones who would realize his dream.

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:11.610
Or perhaps he wanted to believe it.

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:18.910
Siegmeister choosing the 730 Mafia's Bruce Ashbey to lead this group...

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:23.260
...may have affected the course
of each member's life in some way.

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:28.560
Had Jasper or Warwick been selected, I wonder what different path history may have taken.

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:33.510
But it is also true that
with his enormous talent...

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:37.060
...Bruce Ashbey maximized the use of the information from the Empire.

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:42.460
All the information sent by Michaelsen wasn't always accurate or vital.

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:45.330
It was merely a little better than the mixture of wheat and tares.

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:51.020
There's a limit to how much you can do, 
whether you are gathering or relaying information.

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:55.180
And there are cases where circumstances change after the information is sent.

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:59.030
Information is a living organism - 
with a short life span.

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:03.710
What I dare to draw
as a definitive conclusion...

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:07.650
...is that Ashbey was a master at handling the living organism called information.

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:13.700
Ashbey took full advantage of the information that Michaelsen sent Siegmeister.

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:17.660
During this time...

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:22.550
...the intelligence network that Michaelsen and Siegmeister established within the Empire...

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:25.990
...was forced to undergo
some minor changes.

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:30.660
In other words, it ceased to be an organization that offered information to the Alliance...

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:33.260
...and instead became an organization that cooperated with Ashbey's battlefield victories.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:37.260
Was Siegmeister satisfied with that ?

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:42.590
Over the course of those seven years, there was no conflict between the two.

00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:47.710
If the conflict were to have surfaced at some point, it would have been after the 2nd Battle of Tiamat...

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:52.310
...when Ashbey consummated his
promotion through the military ranks.

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:55.310
Then when Ashbey ventured
into the political arena...

00:10:55.310 --> 00:11:00.810
...that conflict would lead either
to resolution or to catastrophe.

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:04.570
Sorry to interrupt.

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:05.770
Please continue.

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:12.140
Needless to say, such a
circumstance never arose.

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:15.050
For Ashbey died in
the 2nd Battle of Tiamat.

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:27.240
At the time of the 2nd Battle of Tiamat,
Space Year 745, Imperial Year 436...

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:35.000
...the Empire must have been suspicious that its military secrets were being leaked to the enemy.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:40.430
It appears that an internal investigation within the military was being carried out in secrecy.

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:45.600
As a result, Michaelsen was beginning to
come under suspicion right before the battle.

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:48.550
But the problem was the issue of the honor of the Empire.

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:52.260
So interrogations and arrests
couldn't be officially made...

00:11:52.260 --> 00:11:56.820
...and Michaelsen didn't
easily betray himself, either.

00:11:56.820 --> 00:12:02.060
Hatred toward Michaelsen and the drive to remove him were strong enough...

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:04.710
...but they couldn't
carry it out officially.

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:12.780
The fact that Kefenhiller was subjected to Admiral Korzel's insinuations just before the 2nd Battle of Tiamat...

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:16.710
...may not be an indication of
an impending purge of Michaelsen...

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:20.310
...but of the intention to
expose all the potential culprits.

00:12:20.310 --> 00:12:25.610
Admiral Korzel himself served as the center figure in the investigation of Michaelsen.

00:12:29.710 --> 00:12:34.160
But Admiral Korzel died
in the 2nd Battle of Tiamat...

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:36.820
...and the investigation of Michaelsen
was suspended for the time being.

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:40.910
For one thing, so many admirals
had died during that battle...

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:46.910
...that the Military Personnel Office had to bring up new officers...

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:51.810
...and couldn't punish an incumbent admiral without firm evidence.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:57.760
And even though they suffered a huge loss,
since their nemesis Ashbey died in the battle...

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:02.490
...and Michaelsen cautiously suspended his organization's activities for the time being...

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:07.150
...the Imperial Force may have decided that the actual impending danger had been removed.

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:13.880
In any case, the management of
this affair was postponed for later.

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:19.160
Of course, Ashbey's death
affected Siegmeister as well.

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:20.360
In his youth...

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:24.720
...he was disappointed with the body politic and social construction of the Galactic Empire...

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:29.970
...and in his adult life, he despaired at the reality of the Free Planets Alliance that was far from ideal.

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:35.460
And Bruce Ashbey's death
and the disbanding of the 730 Mafia...

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:38.180
...may have been the final
psychological blow to Siegmeister.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:44.460
He was 63 years old at the time...

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:48.250
...and though he couldn't be considered to be senile yet, he decided to retire...

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:50.880
...leaving the files he had commissioned in other people's custody...

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:56.290
...and withdrew to a room he rented in a farmhouse about 100 km away from Heinessen.

00:13:56.290 --> 00:13:58.260
Three years later, in 737...

00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:02.370
...he died from complications of pneumonia, without even calling for a doctor.

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:10.210
And what happened to Michaelsen ?

00:14:10.210 --> 00:14:16.510
When things settled down, he restarted the activities of the organization, which he had put in hibernation.

00:14:16.510 --> 00:14:20.860
The activities of his organization were not inferior to what they used to be...

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:24.430
...but the competence of the receiving side
of the information suffered a major drop-off.

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:27.910
Siegmeister was gone, 
and more than anything else...

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:33.530
...Bruce Ashbey, the master at using the information to its fullest, was no longer there either.

00:14:33.530 --> 00:14:36.910
Realizing the decline of his network, Michaelsen apparently wanted to dissolve the organization...

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:43.060
...and leave it to someone else, but a replacement for him wasn't found.

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:47.700
Michaelsen lost his chance to withdraw.

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:55.560
It happened 6 years after the 2nd Battle of Tiamat on October 29th, Imperial Year 442.

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:07.910
On that day, the personnel reassignments of 11,400 officers were to be announced...

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:11.530
...and the Imperial Ministry of the Military was packed with officers.

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:17.550
At 10:30, the first transfers were announced, but those were retracted 20 minutes later...

00:15:17.550 --> 00:15:18.920
...and the initial commotion took place.

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:24.570
The Personnel Department Chief, 
Vice Admiral Myer Hofen was held responsible...

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:28.390
...and he had to apologize
through an in-house broadcast.

00:15:28.390 --> 00:15:30.910
But there were grumbles that
his manner of apology was insolent...

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:32.500
...and denouncements were
again directed his way.

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:35.910
But the commotion
died down before noon...

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:39.390
...and at 13:20, the finalized
first transfers were announced.

00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:43.710
At this time, Vice Admiral Michaelsen peeked out of his Secretarial Office...

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:47.260
...and, looking at the mixed sadness and
happiness among the officers, just shrugged.

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:49.360
There were many people
who observed him then.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:57.890
Following that, the second transfers were announced at 14:30 and the hall was again filled with officers.

00:16:05.510 --> 00:16:14.050
According to the records, only Admiral Steiermark 
met with him that day, but he left the office at 13:15.

00:16:14.050 --> 00:16:19.240
There was testimony that someone in military uniform secretly left the room around 14:00...

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:21.410
...but it had no value as evidence...

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:26.660
...because then, the more than 10,000
people in the building would be suspects.

00:16:26.660 --> 00:16:33.710
In the end, after a long investigation, no culprit has ever been found.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:41.710
That's the summary, as gathered from over 40 years of Christoph von Kefenhiller's research.

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:57.650
But...

00:16:57.650 --> 00:17:02.060
...I don't know how to put it, but well,
it feels like a lie you've just witnessed.

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:04.330
It is a lie.

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:09.740
There's no material evidence.

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:12.850
It's probable, and it's persuasive.

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:16.070
But it's still a hypothesis at this time.

00:17:16.070 --> 00:17:19.300
For that hypothesis to become an
established theory, what would it take ?

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:21.960
A lot more information.

00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:25.860
That's the most important thing.

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:46.060
And the hypothesis about Admiral Ashbey's murder plot - what do you think ?

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:52.710
The murder plot hypothesis would have
been more beneficial to the Imperial side.

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:58.020
To sow a seed of mutual distrust between the government and the Alliance military.

00:17:58.510 --> 00:17:59.260
I see.

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:02.910
But as for the recent letters...

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:07.540
...that was Kefenhiller drawing our attention to the series of events that took place.

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:10.140
I couldn't confirm it with him, but...

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:23.610
Both the Empire and Alliance are hiding many historical facts in the name of military secrecy.

00:18:23.610 --> 00:18:28.260
I'd like to believe that the Alliance is more open, but there's still a lot of room for improvement.

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:31.900
You're right.

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:37.760
And to think of it in reverse, Kefenhiller's
hypothesis is most persuasive right now...

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:43.760
...but if even one of such hidden facts were to be exposed, it could be overturned in the future.

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:50.180
If the complete picture of the whole affair is ever to be disclosed...

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:54.140
...it will only happen after the
present political body collapses.

00:18:54.140 --> 00:18:57.080
When the Empire and
Alliance both cease to exist...

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:02.520
The Hero of El Facil becomes
the Prophet of Heinessen, huh ?

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:12.490
Regardless of the process, I wonder if it's even possible to uncover the truth after so many decades.

00:19:12.490 --> 00:19:16.300
Wouldn't it be impossible unless
the witnesses are still alive ?

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:19.880
No, I don't know if that's quite right.

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:23.350
Rather than the contemporaries who actually witnessed the affair, later generations...

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:29.810
...who have to rely on documents and artifacts often perceive the essence of the affair more easily.

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:33.540
Otherwise, there's no point in the existence of the study of history.

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:41.440
Kefenhiller, while his memory as a participant in the 2nd Battle of Tiamat was still vivid...

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:43.710
...couldn't become a
 perceptive historical observer.

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:49.260
I think that only from the distant perspective of more than 40 years was he able to analyze it objectively.

00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:59.400
Then I will come by and pick up my luggage tomorrow.

00:20:00.180 --> 00:20:01.560
Well, thank you for dinner.

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:11.260
You, Lt. Commander Yang,
and Mr. Attenborough -

00:20:11.260 --> 00:20:15.520
You three are all talented,
but seem to be short-sighted.

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:19.450
You all seem to go your own way despite the obvious drawbacks.

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:21.700
But I guess that's why you all share the same wavelength.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:22.850
"Short-sighted," huh ?

00:20:24.560 --> 00:20:29.950
I don't know about Attenborough, but Yang is a Lt. Commander and I'm a Commander.

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:33.510
For being "short-sighted," we're
fairly well ranked, don't you think ?

00:20:33.510 --> 00:20:34.660
You're right.

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:36.140
You'll be promoted.

00:20:36.140 --> 00:20:38.910
But I'm sure you'll all have to bear
responsibilities beyond your ranks.

00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:40.790
Hey, now.

00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:42.650
Now you're becoming a prophet.

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:53.150
I wonder what we'll be
like in ten or twenty years.

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:59.170
When I think of the 730 Mafia, I start to wonder about that.

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:03.120
No one knows where
he'll be in ten years.

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:06.120
It's better not to know, I think.

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:09.230
If possible, I hope we'll all be alive.

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:14.310
That might be asking for too much.

00:21:14.310 --> 00:21:15.910
For as long as we're in the military.

00:21:17.570 --> 00:21:20.020
Mr. Detective, how are you doing ?

00:21:20.020 --> 00:21:25.770
I'm well, more or less, but I'm troubling many people as I live my life.

00:21:25.770 --> 00:21:31.160
On January 31st, while Yang filed the piles of documents Kefenhiller left...

00:21:31.160 --> 00:21:34.210
...he received a
letter from Miriam Rosas.

00:21:34.210 --> 00:21:37.960
The content, to a certain degree, was what Yang expected.

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:43.240
My grandfather's death was
apparently a semi-conscious suicide.

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:46.060
When he consumed the large
 dose of outdated sleeping pills...

00:21:46.060 --> 00:21:49.500
...he seemed content
either to live or die.

00:21:51.090 --> 00:21:54.600
For many years,
my grandfather wanted to die.

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:57.560
He used to say that since memory was becoming more enjoyable than reality...

00:21:57.560 --> 00:22:01.750
...there was no need
for him to live on.

00:22:02.910 --> 00:22:08.800
Mr. Detective, your visit wasn't the cause, so please don't blame yourself.

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:13.710
It's like I'm contradicting myself,
but I thought I should let you know.

00:22:13.710 --> 00:22:16.990
Certainly, there's no use worrying about it.

00:22:16.990 --> 00:22:19.910
But it's probably certain that
because he talked to me...

00:22:19.910 --> 00:22:24.360
...he decided to depart
on his journey to the past.

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:32.410
In either case, that fact should be stored only in his heart - that was what Yang decided.

00:22:34.270 --> 00:22:39.500
On February 6th, Yang was summoned to the Personnel Department of the Joint Chiefs of Staff Headquarters.

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:41.860
This suggested his assignment would be to front line duty.

00:22:42.760 --> 00:22:45.910
I order Lt. Commander
Yang Wenli to a new assignment.

00:22:45.910 --> 00:22:52.440
It has been decided that as of March 1st, you will be assigned to the 8th Fleet's Strategy Department.

00:22:52.440 --> 00:22:55.540
I expect your best efforts and diligence in the assignment you've been given.

00:22:55.540 --> 00:22:57.770
I humbly acknowledge my assignment.

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:01.350
In other words, my vacation has ended.

00:23:06.150 --> 00:23:10.840
On February 25th,
Alex Cazellnu was married.

00:23:16.950 --> 00:23:18.360
Since I'm assigned
to front line duty...

00:23:18.360 --> 00:23:22.110
...I can't be treated to Mrs. Cazellnu's
homemade cooking for a while.

00:23:23.510 --> 00:23:26.080
It's Senior Yang's turn next.

00:23:26.080 --> 00:23:27.330
Please be sure to invite me.

00:23:34.160 --> 00:23:39.910
The documents Mr. Kefenhiller left have been designated as important intelligence articles.

00:23:39.910 --> 00:23:43.350
In other words, they'll be sealed for another twenty-five years.

00:23:45.950 --> 00:23:48.090
Are you sure you're okay with that ?

00:23:48.090 --> 00:23:52.430
If you had released it under your name, it would have avoided the military secret treatment.

00:23:53.430 --> 00:23:56.710
That was Captain Kefenhiller's research.

00:23:56.710 --> 00:23:59.600
I only summarized it.

00:23:59.600 --> 00:24:05.400
Twenty-five years from now, there will be more talented people who'll establish a firmer theory.

00:24:07.610 --> 00:24:10.910
By that time, both the Empire and
Alliance may have ceased to exist...

00:24:10.910 --> 00:24:13.260
...and many historical
documents may be made public.

00:24:26.810 --> 00:24:31.270
My assignment on Econia
was too good to be a coincidence.

00:24:31.270 --> 00:24:33.510
Perhaps it was
Commander Cazellnu's doing...

00:24:33.510 --> 00:24:38.260
...allowing his junior with aspirations to be a historian a glimpse of his dream life.

00:24:39.860 --> 00:24:44.810
Well, I wonder what the new
assignment in March will bring me.

00:24:46.910 --> 00:24:53.270
In his military life, Yang Wenli would find himself in several ranks.

00:24:53.270 --> 00:24:58.010
The shortest term was
his 6 hours as a Lieutenant...

00:24:58.010 --> 00:25:02.040
...and the longest was 3 years
and 10 months as a Lt. Commander.

00:25:00.120 --> 00:25:04.660
The Journey in Search of the Exit

00:25:05.500 --> 00:25:10.430
Preview of Next Episode

00:25:06.700 --> 00:25:09.500
In July of Imperial Year 482...

00:25:09.500 --> 00:25:12.500
...at the Imperial Force's frontline base on Planet Kapchelanka...

00:25:12.500 --> 00:25:17.700
...two 15-year-old officers, who had just graduated from the Military Cadet School took up their posts.

00:25:17.700 --> 00:25:21.260
Reinhard von Musel and Siegfried Kircheis.

00:25:21.260 --> 00:25:25.260
Their long battle started there.

00:25:25.520 --> 00:25:35.460
Legend of the Galactic Heroes Gaiden

00:25:25.520 --> 00:25:35.460
Valley of White Silver
Chapter I

00:25:31.280 --> 00:25:35.360
My friend, do you remember
those days on the battlefield ?
